 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S444-023\", \"clauses\": {\"represent\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F17\", \"template\": \"Shade {fraction_str} of the shape.\", \"reasoning\": \"F17 is a shade-the-shape task, a model-based representation of a fraction. F17 itself fails Rule 1 (see failing_families), but this clause is producible from it.\"}, \"identify\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F11\", \"template\": \"What fraction does the {name} show?\", \"reasoning\": \"F11 asks the learner to name the fraction a model shows, which is identification. The name slot draws from model_names or model, and its members contain no vocabulary outside the cumulative_vocab or the introduced set.\"}, \"similar_fractions\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F15\", \"template\": \"{unshaded}/{denom}\", \"reasoning\": \"F15 derives its denominator from the keyed answer, so a distractor shares the answer's denominator and forms a like (similar) fraction. The unshaded value is an arithmetic image whose operation the packet does not state, so the family is not judged failing on that ground.\"}, \"denominators_2_3_4_5_6_8\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F08\", \"template\": \"{num}/{den}\", \"reasoning\": \"The den slot draws from the grade's denom_pool, whose members are 2, 3, 4, 5, 6 and 8, exactly the clause's denominators. F08 fails Rule 1 on its numerator domain, not on this clause.\"}, \"groups_of_objects\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F11\", \"template\": \"What fraction does the {name} show?\", \"reasoning\": \"The declared set_model variant is printed as the name set model, which is a groups-of-objects representation. The name slot can print set model.\"}, \"fraction_charts\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F17\", \"template\": \"Shade {fraction_str} of the shape.\", \"reasoning\": \"A fraction chart is a shape divided into equal parts that the learner shades, which is the declared area_model representation printed through F17. F17 fails Rule 1 on its fraction_str values, not on this clause.\"}, \"fraction_tiles\": {\"verdict\": \"NOT_PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": null, \"template\": null, \"reasoning\": \"No family prints fraction tiles. The declared fraction_model variants are area_model, number_line and set_model only, and F11 names are model, number line, set model and shaded picture. Nothing in the packet produces tiles.\"}, \"number_line\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F11\", \"template\": \"What fraction does the {name} show?\", \"reasoning\": \"The name slot can print number line, and the declared number_line variant is a model the learner reads to identify a fraction.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F05\", \"F08\", \"F13\", \"F14\", \"F17\", \"F19\", \"F20\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"So the {frac_lbl} is {num}/{den}.\", \"{num}/{den}\", \"{denom}/{numer}\", \"{numer}/{denom}\", \"Shade {fraction_str} of the shape.\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F08 num domain is 1 to 7 at every denominator in denom_pool (2 to 8), so it can print numerator greater than denominator, for example 5/2 or 7/3, as a keyed answer, distractor or option. Those are improper fractions, a concept on the NOT_YET_KNOWN list and outside the declared bound similar_proper. F20 and F14 print numerator from 1 to 4 and denominator from 3, 4, 5 and 8 as separate observed runs with no stated joint constraint, so 4/3 is not excluded. F05 prints the same pair in a hint. F17 shades fraction_str derived from numerator and denominator, so it can ask a learner to shade a value above one whole. F13 and F19 swap numerator and denominator, and when the numerator is 1 the result is a whole number written as a fraction (denominator 1), outside the denominator set 2, 3, 4, 5, 6 and 8. F09, F11, F04, F06 and F07 stay within the declared bounds on the packet's evidence. F15, F16, F21 and F22 use arithmetic whose operation the packet does not state, and this is noted, not failed.\"}",
